## Remarks

Testing with Microsoft's Pex also supports automatically generating various test parameters based on known categories such as `PexAssumeUnderTest`, `PexCategory`, `PexInlineData`, etc. It can also help to define the `AssumePrecondition` that the contract should be satisfied or not.

Also, it provides `PexObserve` to observe the value or state of variables, and it supports customizing the display name for these variables. This makes the test report more readable.

Debug Assert can be used to write the assertion part too. In this case, we are checking whether the new array contains the element, if it is then the index of the element in the new array should be different then size of the old array. If it is not then it should be the size of the old array.



