### Test Driven Development (TDD) with Pex

Pex can be used in conjunction with Test Driven Development (TDD). With TDD, tests are written before the implementation begins. This encourages you to think about the functionality you are trying to achieve in the test cases. 

As you get your tests written, the Pex plug-in would then generate input parameters for your tests which can be run. You can then make the necessary code changes to pass the tests. This will ensure new code you are writing is robust and as per the requirements.

For example, before you start coding for a new function, you might first write unit tests for the function in Visual Studio. You can use Pex to create random data inputs for these tests. Then you would simply need to implement the function, compiling, and running the tests each time. This iterative development, in combination with Pex, can be very powerful.

### Practical Test Case Design with Pex

Pex is an excellent tool for practicing Test Case Design. It provides a way to understand the requirements thoroughly and design a robust test suite from there.

Pex operates on the principle of exploring state and transition space in order to find valid and invalid tests. When it comes up with a combination of data, it generates a test, executes this test, and based on the result, refines the set of available input values or constraints. This refinement process--------------------	    // an Assertion for New_arrList
